course: dictionary
lesson: 4433
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «A handful of sweets» means the amount you can hold in one hand. «Only a handful of children came» means a small number of children.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. «Only a handful of children came» means only a few children came, and that makes sense. Ask yourself: is the word talking about a hand, a number, or a person?
explain: Informal talk can change the meaning again. «The puppy is a handful» does not mean the puppy fits in one hand. It means the puppy is hard to control, because it is lively and naughty.
fact: A handful means the amount you can hold in one hand, such as «a handful of sweets».
fact: A handful can also mean a small number, as in «Only a handful of children came».
fact: In informal talk, «a real handful» or «The puppy is a handful» means someone or something that is hard to control.
fact: In cooking and science, «a handful» is a rough measure, not an exact one.
fact: Sharks kill «only a handful of people» a year, so here handful means a small number.
exercise: «A handful of sweets» means what? | A large box of sweets | *The amount you can hold in one hand | A rough number of hours | A sweet shop
exercise: «Only a handful of children came to the party.» What does handful mean here? | The amount in one hand | A child who is hard to control | A whole class | *A small number
exercise: The recipe says «add a handful of raisins». How exact is this measure? | An exact number of raisins | *A rough amount, not exact | Exactly one raisin | An exact weight in grams
test: «A female common frog lays 1,000 to 2,000 eggs, and often only a handful become adult frogs.» In this sentence, handful means | Exactly five frogs | *A small number | The amount in one hand | A jelly clump
test: Which sentence uses handful to mean a lively, naughty child or pet? | «Add a handful of soil to the pot.» | *«Our new kitten is a real handful.» | «She ate a handful of crisps.» | «Only a handful of guests stayed.»
exam: In «A single handful of healthy soil holds more living things than there are people on Earth», what does handful mean? | *The amount you can hold in one hand | A small number of people | A naughty child | A fixed number of grams
